.SH NAME
ssoossh-host - Manage local sshd principal mapping, and check sshd's setup.


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBssoossh host [command] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Configures the principal mapping used when sshd asks for authorized principals via AuthorizedPrincipalsCommand, and checks that this host's sshd will accept ssoossh certificates. The mapping is managed locally and never fetched from the server.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--file\fP="/etc/ssoossh/principals.yaml"
	path to the local principal mapping file (YAML: local account -> list of principals)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for host


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP=""
	path to the ssoossh config file

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	server address including scheme (e.g. "https://example.com") assumes https if omited.

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	trace what the command is doing, to stderr; repeat for more (-v steps, -vv requests and files, -vvv bodies)


